  <section id="pg-ranks" class="pg hidden"><div class="sheet"><h2>LEVEL & RANKED</h2><div id="rankHead"></div><div id="rankList"></div></div></section>
  <section id="pg-news" class="pg hidden"><div class="sheet news">
    <h2>NEWS</h2>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 1.02 · NEW BATTLE ROYALE TOWNS</div><ul><li><b>All island houses rebuilt</b> in five types: tiled-roof cottages, two-storey houses with balconies, flat-roof villas with stairs up to the roof, three-storey apartment blocks in the towns, and shops with big windows and awnings.</li><li>Inside every house: rooms split by walls with doorways, proper staircases, rails, open doors, and furniture to use as cover: beds, sofas, kitchen counters, fridges, wardrobes, desks and tables.</li><li>Rooftops you can fight from: villas and apartments have a stair hut on the roof, a parapet, water tanks and loot.</li><li>Outside details: glass in the windows, shutters, window trims, porches, canopies, chimneys, drainpipes and AC units.</li><li><b>Walled compounds</b> with gates around many houses, often with a parked car inside for cover.</li><li>More loot spots, spread over every room and floor.</li><li><b>New trees:</b> full leafy crowns instead of round blobs, plus pines, birches, olive trees and better palms. Each map gets its own mix, and the island has small forests to hide in.</li></ul><div class="tag">PATCH 1.01 · BUILDINGS YOU CAN ENTER</div><ul><li><b>New barn:</b> walk in through the big sliding doors, the side door or the back door. Hay loft with a ladder, stalls, hay bales for cover and loot inside. The roof now sits properly on the walls.</li><li><b>Airfield control tower:</b> door at the bottom and a ladder up to the glass cab at the top.</li><li><b>Military base:</b> watch towers have ladders and railings, and the tents are open so you can walk in.</li><li><b>Radio Hill:</b> the control hut is now a real hut with a door and windows.</li><li><b>Reactor map:</b> the farm is replaced by a <b>Reactor Plant</b>. Walk into the reactor building and under the cooling towers, and climb the catwalk in the turbine hall. There is also a transformer yard, a vent stack and an office.</li><li>Place names and trees now match each map: no more palm trees next to a reactor or in Ukraine.</li></ul><div class="tag">PATCH 1.00 · THE NEW STORE + LIQUID GLASS</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Featured Today</b>: a big banner at the top of the store shows the best daily skin, floating over a glowing spotlight in its rarity colour, with its price and a countdown.</li>
      <li><b>Item preview</b>: tap any item to open it in a big preview. Gun skins and agents spin in <b>live 3D</b> (drag to turn them), with the rarity, a description, the price and your balance after buying.</li>
      <li><b>No more accidental buys</b>: you now confirm every purchase with a big BUY button. A PURCHASED! burst follows, and you can <b>EQUIP</b> the item straight from the store.</li>
      <li><b>New item cards</b> with a rarity tag, a coloured glow behind the item, a rarity strip at the bottom, and a light that follows your mouse while the card tilts in 3D.</li>
      <li><b>Liquid glass</b>: the store tabs, coin balance, featured banner, item preview, HUD health and ammo cards, top menu bar, pause menu and case opening window now use frosted, see-through glass with a bright rim and sheen.</li>
      <li>The Daily tab shows a green dot while today's free finisher is still unclaimed.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.99 · BETTER UI</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>New in-game HUD.</b> Health and armour sit in one glass card with a thick segmented health bar (green, turning red when you are low) and a blue armour bar. Your medkit count shows as a small chip.</li>
      <li>The ammo counter is a matching card with a bigger number. Money, the buy hint and the kill feed got the same look, and new kills slide in.</li>
      <li><b>Settings</b>: every option is its own row, with switch toggles instead of tick boxes, sliders that fill as you drag, and cleaner drop-downs.</li>
      <li><b>News</b>: each patch is a card you can open and close, with a version badge. The newest is marked NEW.</li>
      <li><b>Store and inventory</b>: cards lift and glow in their rarity colour when you hover over them, buttons press in, and the scrollbars are slimmer.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.98 · CASE OPENING ANIMATION</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>New case opening animation.</b> Your 3D case drops in and lands, rattles harder and harder, the latches pop, and the lid swings open. Light pours out in the colour of the item's rarity, with a flash of rays.</li>
      <li>Then the reel spins as before. The winning item pops out with a glow in its rarity colour, plus a bigger fanfare for Legendary and rarer drops.</li>
      <li>New sounds for every step: the landing, the rattle, the latches, the lid opening, the burst and the reveal. Tap the case to skip straight to the reel.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.97 · NO MORE OVERLAPPING WALLS</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Fixed objects and walls clipping into each other on Crossroads. Buildings that stand side by side no longer put doors, windows, balconies, AC units, pipes, corner stones or ivy on the walls they share, and their trim bands and roof edges stop at the neighbouring wall.</li>
      <li>Tiled roofs (Vineyard) are only added where they don't poke into a taller building next door.</li>
      <li>The B Hall roof now sits neatly inside its walls, and the B Halls corridor roof, arches and gate fit exactly.</li>
      <li>Lost Temple pools and the second row of sandbags can no longer be placed partly inside walls.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.96 · NEW MAP: CROSSROADS</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>The whole map is new.</b> The old three-lane layout is gone; Bomb Defusal, Team Deathmatch and Free For All now play on <b>Crossroads</b>, in every map theme.</li>
      <li><b>A Main</b>: from T spawn take the west street into a long corridor with doors, through a small yard and a gate into the open <b>A Courtyard</b>.</li>
      <li><b>Mid</b>: a street with double doors leads to the central <b>Plaza</b> with a monument in the middle. The <b>Market Alley</b> links the plaza to A Main.</li>
      <li><b>B Halls</b>: from T spawn take the east street into a roofed corridor that opens into the big covered <b>B Hall</b>, with pillars and lamps.</li>
      <li>From the plaza, the <b>A Connector</b> arch leads into A and the <b>B Garage</b> arch into B. A narrow <b>CT Mid</b> alley with a door runs down to the CT street.</li>
      <li><b>CT side</b>: a street along the south links CT spawn to one entrance into each site. Bots know every route.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.95 · BETTER MAP LAYOUT</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Both bomb sites are now enclosed.</b> Each has a back building and a wall on the CT side, so there are three ways in: the long route, the short route from Mid, and one 10 m CT entrance. No more walking in from anywhere.</li>
      <li><b>New Lower Tunnel</b>: a roofed alley from Mid straight into the B tunnels, a new route for rotating or flanking.</li>
      <li><b>T spawn</b> is no longer one huge open strip: two houses, short walls and crates split it into separate Long, Mid and Tunnels exits.</li>
      <li>Closed off the dead-end corners at the end of Long A, the tunnels and the CT corners, and added cover at the CT entrances and in lower Mid to break the long A to B sightline.</li>
      <li>Bots know all the new routes. Works on every map theme (Dunehold, Oasis, Vineyard, Lost Temple, Pharaoh, Exclusion Zone, Reactor) in Bomb Defusal, Team Deathmatch and Free For All.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.94 · UNLOCK THE GUN FIRST</div>
    <ul>
      <li>You now have to <b>unlock a gun before you can get its skins</b>. In the Store's Skins tab, locked guns show a lock, their skins say <b>LOCKED</b>, and an <b>UNLOCK GUN</b> button lets you buy the gun right there.</li>
      <li><b>Cases only drop skins for guns you have unlocked.</b> Each case shows how many of its skins you can win. If you have none of its guns yet, unlock one in the Armory first.</li>
      <li>Daily skins, the weekly Care Package and daily-task skin rewards also only offer skins for unlocked guns. Skins you already own are kept.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.93 · GRENADE FX</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Frag grenade</b>: new BGMI-style explosion with a starburst flash, rolling fireball, a dust ring that kicks out along the ground, a shockwave, a thick smoke column, a burnt scorch mark, flying dirt and glowing sparks. Heavier screen shake and an orange flash when it goes off close to you.</li>
      <li><b>New explosion sound</b>: a sharp crack, a deep boom, a rumbling tail and falling debris. Get caught close and your ears ring while the world sounds muffled for a few seconds.</li>
      <li><b>Molotov / Incendiary</b>: glass shatters, burning fuel splashes out, and the fire now has flickering animated flames, glowing embers on the ground and black smoke. You hear a fire roar with crackles, and the screen glows orange while you stand in the flames.</li>
      <li><b>Smoke grenade</b>: a thick white cloud that billows out from the canister and slowly breaks up, with a pop and a long gas hiss.</li>
      <li><b>Faster sniper reloads</b>: AWP, SSG 08, Barrett M82, SCAR-20 and G3SG1 now reload in <b>0.82 s</b> (bolt time between shots is unchanged).</li>
      <li><b>Grenade warning</b>: a red marker with the distance shows nearby grenades and molotovs, even ones behind you.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.92 · AGENT PRICES</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Every <b>character (agent)</b> now costs <b>200 coins more</b> in the Store: Sand Viper and Jungle Ghost 1,100, Night Owl and Arctic Fox 1,700, Crimson Fang 2,800, Gold Standard 5,200. Operator is still free, and rank-reward characters are unchanged.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.91 · GOLDEN CASE</div>
    <ul>
      <li>New <b>Golden Case</b> (5,000 coins): every skin inside is a <b>24K Gold</b> gun skin, any gun in the game. Find it in the Cases tab of the Store.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.90 · CASE-ONLY SKINS</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Skins that come from cases can no longer be bought in the shop.</b> In the Skins tab they now show <b>CASE ONLY</b>, and the Daily skins never offer them. Open the case to win them.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.89 · RANK REWARDS &amp; REAL GROUND</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Rank rewards:</b> from <b>Platinum</b> up, every rank step gives a prize: <b>characters</b> (Night Owl, Arctic Fox, Crimson Fang, Gold Standard), <b>redeem codes</b> with coins, and <b>skins</b> (AK-47 | Neon Rush, M4A4, AWP, 24K Gold AK-47). Open <b>Ranks</b> and press <b>CLAIM</b>. Rewards use your peak rank, so you keep them if you drop.</li>
      <li>The top rank is now called <b>Legend</b>.</li>
      <li><b>Realistic grass and sand:</b> lawns now mix lush grass, dry patches and bare earth with tiny wild flowers and finer blades. Sand has wind ripples, fine grain, sparkles and scattered pebbles, and the island beach uses the same photo sand with wet darkening near the water. Detail scales with your graphics setting.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.88 · ELITE CASE</div>
    <ul>
      <li>The <b>Horizens Elite Case</b> has a new premium design: carbon-fibre black shell, gold armoured corners, a gold handle, four gold latches, a glowing red seam and an ELITE plate on the lid.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.87 · 3D CASES</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Cases are now real 3D hard-shell cases</b> with a carry handle, latches, ribbed panels and a padlock. Hover over one (or drag it with your finger) to spin it around. Each case has its own colour, and the three best items inside are shown under it.</li>
      <li>Clicking the case itself no longer spends coins by accident; only the price button opens it.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.86 · NEW SHOP</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Brand-new Shop:</b> a tab bar across the top (Home, Cases, Skins, Daily, More) with a big close button. Every item is now a colour-coded card: the colour shows its rarity, the name is on top and the price sits on a yellow coin button at the bottom.</li>
      <li><b>Daily tab:</b> five weapon skins, five agents and a Finishers row that change every day. One finisher each day is <b>FREE</b>. The timer shows when the shop refreshes (midnight UTC), and the yellow refresh button lets you re-roll the picks up to 3 times a day.</li>
      <li><b>Skins tab:</b> pick any weapon and browse every skin for it. <b>More tab:</b> all agents, knife skins, katanas and blade finishes. The Weekly Care Package and the redeem-code box are on the Home tab.</li>
      <li>Items you already own now show <b>OWNED</b> instead of letting you buy them twice.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.85 · FAIR PLAY &amp; SMOOTH PLAY</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Anti-cheat referee:</b> in online rooms the host now checks every hit before it counts: your fire rate, the weapon you hold, where you were standing, whether your bullet actually passed through the target (as it was moving, adjusted for lag), whether a wall was in the way, and the damage, which now comes from the weapon table instead of from the shooter. Speed, teleport, fly and flood checks pull cheaters back; repeat offenders are ignored, then removed from the match.</li>
      <li><b>Ping:</b> live ping on the HUD and in the scoreboard. The host rewinds enemy positions to what your screen showed, so shots land at high ping too, and other players glide a little closer to where they really are.</li>
      <li><b>Battery Saver</b> (Settings → Video): 30 FPS cap, lower resolution and lighter effects; Auto turns it on at 20% battery. <b>Adaptive resolution</b> now works with every graphics preset. Far-away and off-screen soldiers animate at a lower rate, which saves a lot of CPU on phones.</li>
      <li><b>Daily Mutators:</b> a new twist every day for everyone: Low Gravity, Glass Cannon, Big Heads, Speed Rush, Vampire or Fog of War. Switch it on or off on the Play tab; your first match of the day gives <b>+250 XP</b>. Ranked and Defuse never use mutators.</li>
      <li>Online rooms are still hosted on a player's device, so the host is trusted; dedicated ranked servers are the next step.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.84 · GRAPHICS 2.0 &amp; NEW RELOADS</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Post-processing:</b> real bloom (the sun, lights, muzzle flashes and signs glow), cinematic ACES colour grading, sharpening, a lens vignette, subtle film grain and colour fringing at the edges. It's on automatically for capable devices, and you can change it in Settings → Video → Post-processing.</li>
      <li><b>Wind-blown grass</b> on the Battle Royale island: thousands of swaying blades around you that fade out smoothly in the distance. Auto graphics thins or removes it on slower phones.</li>
      <li><b>New reload animation:</b> the gun rolls to show the magazine well, the old magazine drops out, your support hand fetches a fresh one and slaps it in, pulls the charging handle (or racks the slide on pistols), and the gun settles back with weight. It's synced to the reload sounds.</li>
      <li>The Battle Royale map is now called <b>Horizon Island</b>.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.83 · EVERYTHING BETTER</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Boot Camp:</b> a 2-minute guided tutorial (move, look, shoot, aim, reload, switch weapons, jump and crouch, heal), with keyboard or touch instructions for your device. New players are offered it, and finishing it gives <b>+300 coins</b>. Replay it any time with 🎓 Boot Camp on the home screen.</li>
      <li><b>Customize your touch layout</b> (Settings → Controller &amp; touch): drag any button to move it, change its size, and set the opacity of all buttons. Saved on your device.</li>
      <li><b>More reliable:</b> an error during a match no longer freezes the screen. The game keeps running, and if something keeps failing a window offers to take you back to the menu.</li>
      <li>Damage numbers on by default (headshots in gold), an "R RELOAD" prompt when your magazine runs low, and a 🎨 Customize shortcut on the home screen.</li>
      <li>Results screen: numbers count up, the XP bar fills, a gold VICTORY title, and confetti when you win.</li>
      <li>Battle Royale: the empty team boxes beside the top bar are gone.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.82 · HOTFIX</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Fixed the lobby warning "THREE.CapsuleGeometry is not a constructor". It stopped the lobby setup halfway, so the circling helicopter and the blue rim light never appeared. Both show now.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.81 · UI 2.0</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>START button</b> on the home screen with your current mode (tap the mode card to change it). It starts with your gang when you're the leader.</li>
      <li>New display font, a glowing bar that slides under the active tab, glass panels, and buttons that lift, shine and press.</li>
      <li>Mode cards show map art, and pages and pop-ups animate in.</li>
      <li><b>Compass</b> at the top of the match screen with heading and degrees. In Battle Royale it marks the zone and your squad.</li>
      <li>Phone layout tidied: your name card moves left and START sits bottom-right.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.80 · BETTER LOBBY &amp; A REAL ISLAND</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Battle Royale island:</b> 9 named places, each with its own landmark: Harbor (container yard, gantry crane, pier, fishing boat), Lighthouse Point (rotating light beams), Airfield (runway, hangar with a plane, control tower, fuel tanks), Military Base (walls, watchtowers, barracks, tents), Sunset Farm (barn, silo, fields, windmill), Radio Hill (blinking radio mast), Old Town (water tower), Palm Village and Market Square (stalls around a fountain).</li>
      <li>Dirt roads connect the places. Most houses now stand in the towns instead of being scattered, and a "📍 place name" banner appears when you arrive.</li>
      <li><b>Island map:</b> press M (or tap the minimap) for a full map with place names, roads, the zone and the next circle, the plane's route and your squad. Place names also show on the minimap.</li>
      <li><b>Lobby:</b> warm string lights over the street, game banners on the walls, a parked jeep, sandbags, a helicopter circling overhead, and a cool rim light so soldiers stand out.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.79 · HOTFIX</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Fixed soldiers' heads twisting around in the lobby (the relaxed rifle-carry pose was adding to the new idle look-around every frame).</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.78 · NEW ANIMATIONS &amp; BIGGER BATTLE ROYALE</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>New character animation:</b> feet stay planted (no sliding or floating), and stride length grows with speed with a smooth walk-to-run blend.</li>
      <li>Soldiers step sideways and backwards for real, hips twist toward the movement while the chest keeps aiming, and the body shifts weight, leans into turns and leans when speeding up or braking.</li>
      <li>New ankle joints keep boots flat with heel strike and toe push-off. Soldiers shuffle their feet when turning on the spot, turn smoothly instead of snapping, and breathe and look around when idle.</li>
      <li><b>Battle Royale map 2.5× bigger</b> (more villages, more ground to cover). The zone circles scale with it, so the 20-minute timeline stays the same.</li>
      <li>About: new "Support us on Product Hunt" button next to Telegram.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.77 · GANG, VOICE CHAT &amp; SMOOTHER</div>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Gang:</b> tap ＋ INVITE next to your operator (or ＋ Gang in Friends) to squad up with up to 3 friends. They stand with you in the lobby with their name, level and mic status.</li>
      <li>The gang leader picks any mode and everyone joins the same match automatically, on the same team. In Battle Royale the gang is one squad: no friendly fire, last squad standing wins.</li>
      <li><b>Voice chat:</b> press 🎙 Mic in the gang panel (or N / the mic button in a match) to talk to your gang. 🔊 mutes everyone.</li>
      <li><b>Reload fix:</b> R and fire now cancel a medkit instead of being ignored, "No spare ammo" is shown when you're out, and the Zeus can no longer get stuck mid-reload.</li>
      <li><b>Smoother:</b> Graphics now defaults to Auto. It lowers quality and render resolution on slow devices and raises them when there's headroom. Shadows follow the quality level, and phones skip anti-aliasing.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.76 · NO BUYING IN VERSUS</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Versus (1v1 and 2v2–5v5) no longer has a buy menu, Buy button or money. Everyone fights with the loadout equipped in the Armory.</li>
      <li>Buying still works in Practice, regular Team Deathmatch and Defuse.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.75 · 20-MINUTE BATTLE ROYALE</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Battle Royale now runs on a strict 20:00 timeline. The top bar shows a MATCH countdown from 20:00 to 0:00.</li>
      <li>Phase 1 Early Game: 3:00 looting, then the zone shrinks for 2:00 (5:00 elapsed). Phase 2 Mid Game: 2:00 wait, 1:30 shrink (8:30).</li>
      <li>Phase 3 Engagement: 1:30 wait, 1:30 shrink (11:30). Phase 4 Late Game: 1:00 wait, 1:00 shrink (13:30).</li>
      <li>Phase 5 Final Showdown: 0:30 wait, then the circle closes all the way to nothing over 6:00 (20:00).</li>
      <li>Zone damage rises every phase: 1, 3, 6, 10, 15 HP per second. Every new circle is always inside the current one.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.74 · BOT HEADSHOTS</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Bot headshot rate is now fixed by difficulty: Easy 0%, Medium 20%, Hard 45% of their hits land on the head.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.73 · 360 HP BATTLE ROYALE</div>
    <ul>
      <li>In Battle Royale everyone now has 360 HP (other modes stay at 100). Bots scale too: Rusher 306, Tactical 360, Heavy 540.</li>
      <li>Medkits heal to the full 360, and the zone and fall damage are scaled up so the zone still pushes you.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.72 · HELMET FIT</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Helmets are now sized to the head: smaller shell, tighter brim and band, no more gap above the face.</li>
      <li>The headset earcups sit on the ears and a single mic boom runs to the mouth.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.71 · SUNGLASSES</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Every soldier now wears wrap-around sunglasses with tinted lenses, a frame and arms back to the ears.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.70 · REALISTIC FACES</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Every soldier has a new, more realistic head: shaped jaw and chin, cheekbones, a real nose, eyes with irises and eyelids, eyebrows, lips, ears and stubble.</li>
      <li>The tinted glasses are gone so you can see their faces, and the neck scarf is slimmer.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.69 · EQUIP GUNS</div>
    <ul>
      <li>New Equip button for guns in the Armory. The rifle, SMG, sniper or heavy gun you equip is the one you spawn with in Team Deathmatch, Free For All, Versus and Practice. Equip a pistol to replace the Glock as your sidearm.</li>
      <li>Gun prices are 200 coins higher: 300 to about 700 coins.</li>
      <li>Fixed: the stats panel in the Armory could be cut off at some window sizes.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.68 · AIMING FIX</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Fixed: aiming down sights with guns like the FAMAS put a big block of the gun (carry handle, sight) in the middle of the screen. Every gun now sits just below your crosshair when aiming, so the centre stays clear.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.67 · TELEGRAM</div>
    <ul>
      <li>Join the Combat Horizens Telegram: click the logo in the About screen, or use the new "Join us on Telegram" button.</li>
      <li>The Android app now opens outside links in Telegram or your browser instead of inside the game.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.66 · BUY GUNS</div>
    <h3>Unlock guns with coins</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Open the Armory and press Buy to unlock a gun with coins. Prices run from 300 to about 700 coins.</li>
      <li>Free from the start: Glock-18, USP-45, P2000, P250, AK-47, M4A4, M4A1 SD, AWP, MP9 and MAC-10. Guns you have already got kills with stay unlocked.</li>
      <li>Locked guns show "Armory" in the buy menu. You can still try every gun in Target Practice and pick any gun up in Battle Royale.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.65 · NEW INVENTORY</div>
    <h3>The Armory</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The Inventory is now an armory: pick a category on the left, see the weapon in 3D in the middle (drag to spin it) and its stats on the right.</li>
      <li>Every weapon has a level: 10 kills per level, up to 50, with Bronze, Silver and Gold mastery.</li>
      <li>"Your Performance" shows the matches, kills, headshots, accuracy and damage you've done with each weapon.</li>
      <li>Skins, Equip and Loadout are on the bottom bar. "All items" opens the full item grid.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.64 · MAP VOTE · BETTER SCOPES</div>
    <h3>Map vote in Versus</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Before every Versus match, everyone votes for a map or Random. 10-second timer; it ends early once everyone has voted.</li>
      <li>Bots vote too, and online the host shares every vote with the whole lobby.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Scopes</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>SG 553 and AUG now use a clean red-dot sight with no black mask.</li>
      <li>Sniper scopes are much wider, with a soft edge and a thin reticle with range dots.</li>
      <li>The M1A has its own marksman scope with a red chevron.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.63 · NEW NAMES</div>
    <h3>Renamed maps, weapons and skins</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Maps: Dunehold, Oasis, Vineyard, Lost Temple, Pharaoh, Exclusion Zone and Reactor.</li>
      <li>Weapons: USP-45, M4A1 SD, .357 Revolver and Stun Gun.</li>
      <li>Knife finishes have new names. Credits now list each creator.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.62 · BIGGER ISLAND · 30–35 PLAYERS · NEW PLANE</div>
    <h3>Battle Royale</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The island is about twice as big, with twice as many houses, cover, trees and loot.</li>
      <li>30 to 35 players drop into every match.</li>
      <li>A longer flight and an extra zone phase to suit the bigger map. Ranked and XP placement rewards now scale for 35 players.</li>
      <li>New drop plane: a four-engine transport with spinning propellers, cockpit glass, Combat Horizens livery, an open cargo ramp and flashing navigation lights.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.61 · RANKED · LEVEL 20 UNLOCK</div>
    <h3>Level and Rank are separate now</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Levels only track XP. Reaching Level 20 unlocks <b>Ranked</b>.</li>
      <li>Two ranked ladders: <b>Battle Royale</b> and <b>Team Deathmatch</b>. Bronze, Silver, Gold, Platinum, Diamond, Heroic, Legend. From Platinum up, ranks give rewards: a character, redeem codes and skins.</li>
      <li>Play ranked online or with bots: both add RP (bots give 60%). Ranked bots get tougher as your rank goes up.</li>
      <li>Ranked online rooms need Level 20. Leaving a ranked match early costs RP.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.60 · 4K · SMARTER BOTS · SMALL MAPS</div>
    <h3>4K graphics</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>New 4K Ultra render resolution (Settings, Video): the game is drawn at 3840×2160 and scaled to your screen, so it's sharper even on a 1080p monitor. Also 1440p and Native.</li>
      <li>All wall, ground, brick, rock and sand textures are now 2K, four times sharper than before. Phones automatically use a lighter version.</li>
      <li>New Ultra (8K) shadow quality.</li>
      <li>On a PC with a strong graphics card, 4K Ultra and 8K shadows switch on automatically the first time you play.</li>
      <li>The loading screen artwork is now 4K.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Bots play like humans</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Bots no longer one-tap you out of nowhere. Their aim starts off and settles over about half a second, they need time to turn, and they mostly aim at the chest. Headshots only come when they've lined up well.</li>
      <li>Recoil climbs during long bursts, shooting while moving is inaccurate (so they stop to shoot, like real players), and getting hit throws their aim off.</li>
      <li>Every bot has its own skill level, and distance really matters now.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Smaller maps for small fights</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>1v1, 1v2, 2v2 and the FFA duel now take place on a compact arena (about 40 to 52 m across) instead of the full 100 m map. 3v3 and bigger keep the full map.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.59 · MUSIC</div>
    <h3>Loading screen and lobby music</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>New original music. "Horizon Rising" plays on the loading screen: a slow cinematic theme with deep strings, taiko drums and a shimmering arpeggio.</li>
      <li>"Rally Point" plays in the lobby: a tactical groove with drums, bass, chords and a lead melody that comes in on the second half of the loop.</li>
      <li>The loading theme blends smoothly into the lobby theme. The music fades out when a match starts and comes back when you return to the menu.</li>
      <li>Turn it on or off in Settings, Sound &amp; screen, Music. There is also a separate Music volume slider.</li>
      <li>In a web browser the music starts the first time you tap or click. In the Android app it starts straight away.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.58 · NEW LOADING SCREEN</div>
    <h3>Cinematic loading screen</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The loading screen now shows a real scene from the game, the squad in the street at sunset, with a slow camera push-in.</li>
      <li>Big, sharp logo with the tagline "Every street is a battlefield".</li>
      <li>Glowing embers drifting up, soft light rays, a glass progress panel and tips that fade in and out.</li>
      <li>A smooth zoom-and-fade into the menu when loading finishes. Works on phones in both portrait and landscape.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.57 · ISLAND BATTLE ROYALE</div>
    <h3>Battle Royale on an island</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Battle Royale now takes place on an island surrounded by open sea, Free Fire style: sandy beaches, turquoise shallows, deep blue ocean with waves, sun glint and shoreline foam, palm trees along the coast and rocks on the shore.</li>
      <li>Every house can be entered: doors, windows you can see and shoot through, furniture (beds, tables with chairs, bookshelves, sofas, rugs) and loot inside.</li>
      <li>Two-storey houses with a staircase to the upper floor.</li>
      <li>The zone always closes on land, loot never spawns in the sea, and the minimap shows the island and the water.</li>
      <li>Fixed: bots that landed on a roof walked straight off it and kept walking in mid-air. Bots now fall off ledges and roofs like players do.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.56 · KEVLAR VEST</div>
    <h3>A real Kevlar vest</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>New 3D Kevlar vest model: shaped front and back panels that wrap around the body, woven fabric with stitching, padded shoulder straps, side straps with buckles, MOLLE webbing, a raised armor-plate pocket, three magazine pouches, a KEVLAR name tape and a drag handle on the back.</li>
      <li>The buy menu shows the vest instead of a shield symbol.</li>
      <li>Armor pickups in Battle Royale are now the vest lying flat on the ground.</li>
      <li>The HUD armor icon is now a vest.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.55 · HEADSHOT FIX</div>
    <h3>Headshots always count</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Fixed: shots into the camo leaves on top of Tactical soldiers' helmets passed straight through and did nothing. Head gear on every bot (camo, bandanas, visors) now counts as a headshot.</li>
      <li>Every soldier has a slightly larger head hitbox, so shots that clip the edge of the helmet or the ears register as headshots.</li>
      <li>The neck, shoulders and chest still count as body shots.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.54 · LOADOUT FIX</div>
    <h3>Spawn weapon fix</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Fixed: unequipping the AWP in your Inventory still made you spawn with it in Free For All and Team Deathmatch. Unequipping it now switches you back to the AK-47.</li>
      <li>Equipping an AK-47 or AWP skin in your Inventory also makes it your spawn weapon.</li>
      <li>Changing your spawn weapon during a match now takes effect on your next respawn. A gun you bought or picked up is still kept.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.53 · CLEANER MEDKIT</div>
    <h3>Smoother medkit, 6 second heal</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Healing now takes 6 seconds. The quick moves stay quick; the extra time is a slow injection where you watch the green liquid drain.</li>
      <li>Reworked animation: smooth, flowing motion instead of stopping at each step, with a soft settle when the case comes up and a bounce on the lid.</li>
      <li>The syringe springs up out of its slot when the lid opens, and your hand grabs it without any jump or twist.</li>
      <li>Your left arm now always comes up from below instead of sweeping across the screen.</li>
      <li>A quick jab into your leg, then a slow plunger push with a slight hand tremble.</li>
      <li>The HEALING bar now tracks the injection and disappears once the heal lands.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.52 · MEDKIT</div>
    <h3>Medkit: full heal</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>New Medkit heals you to 100 HP. Press <kbd>H</kbd> (or <kbd>6</kbd>, or tap the red ✚ button on phones).</li>
      <li>Full first-person animation: your gun drops, you raise a red first-aid case, flip the lid, take out the syringe, inject it and toss it, then snap the case shut.</li>
      <li>You spawn with 1 medkit every life. Buy more in the Gear tab for $400 (carry up to 2; up to 5 in Battle Royale).</li>
      <li>Shooting or switching weapons before the injection cancels it, and you keep the medkit.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.51 · REAL SHADOWS</div>
    <h3>Shadows, fixed properly</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Fixed a long-standing bug where sun shadows only appeared in a tiny patch around you. They now cover the whole area you can see.</li>
      <li>Lower afternoon sun: buildings and walls throw long shadows across the streets.</li>
      <li>Shadows no longer shimmer or crawl when you move.</li>
      <li>Shaded areas are deeper and slightly cool-tinted, like real outdoor shade.</li>
      <li>The hard-edged grey bands around walls and crates are gone, replaced by smooth, soft shading where objects meet the ground.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.50 · GROUNDED MAPS</div>
    <h3>Maps that feel solid</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Soft contact shadows where walls, buildings, crates and sandbags meet the ground, so nothing looks like it's floating.</li>
      <li>Darker corners where two walls meet.</li>
      <li>Dirt, grime and sun-bleached patches on the ground break up the repeating floor texture.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.49 · LIVING SKY</div>
    <h3>A real sky</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Every map now has a real sky: deep blue overhead, fading into the haze at the horizon, with soft clouds that slowly drift.</li>
      <li>The sun is visible in the sky and matches the direction of the shadows.</li>
      <li>Looking toward the sun gives a warm glare and lens streak. Buildings in the way block it.</li>
      <li>The film-style vignette from 0.48 now actually shows.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.48 · HIGH GRAPHICS</div>
    <h3>Everything on High</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>High graphics is now the default on every device, phones included.</li>
      <li>Film-style lighting with softer highlights, richer colour and a subtle vignette.</li>
      <li>Very high shadows, high detail, 16x texture filtering and full effects out of the box.</li>
      <li>If a device runs slowly, the game suggests lowering graphics instead of doing it silently.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.47 · REAL TEXTURES</div>
    <h3>Photo-real surfaces</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>New photo-scanned textures (CC0, from ambientCG) on the sand ground, plaster, stone and concrete walls, Vineyard's bricks and cobbled streets, Lost Temple's grass, wooden crates and doors, and the metal ladders.</li>
      <li>On Medium and High graphics, surfaces also get depth: bricks, cobbles, rock and plaster catch the light and throw small shadows. Low graphics keeps the photo textures without depth, to stay fast on phones.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.46 · ARMS</div>
    <h3>No more block arms on any gun</h3>
    <ul><li>The AK-47, AWP, Glock-18, USP-45, P250, Tec-9, MAC-10 and MP9 had square arms built into their models. They now have rounded camo sleeves with cuffs and gloved fists, and still move with every reload and draw animation. Knives and push daggers got gloved hands too.</li></ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.45 · FIX</div>
    <h3>Results screen buttons on phones</h3>
    <ul><li>On phones held sideways, "Play again" and "Main menu" were pushed off the bottom of the results screen. The screen now uses two columns there (result and stats on the left, XP and buttons on the right), and the buttons always stay visible at the bottom.</li></ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.44 · WEAPON WEIGHT</div>
    <h3>Heavy guns slow you down</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>New setting: <b>Settings → Game → Weapon weight affects speed</b>.</li>
      <li><b>Off:</b> you move at the same speed whatever you hold. <b>Normal:</b> heavy guns are a bit slower (the old behaviour). <b>Realistic:</b> machine guns and snipers are much slower, pistols are quick and the knife is fastest.</li>
      <li>The speed line above your ammo now shows <b style="color:#7dd87d">LIGHT</b>, <b style="color:#ffd24a">MEDIUM</b> or <b style="color:#ff8a5a">HEAVY</b> for the weapon in your hand.</li>
      <li>Online matches always use Normal so everyone moves fairly.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.43 · WIN STREAKS</div>
    <h3>Win streaks 🔥</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Win 2 matches in a row to reach <b>Streak 1</b>, 4 in a row for <b>Streak 2</b>, and so on. Losing a match resets it.</li>
      <li>Each new streak level pays coins (100 × the level, up to 400).</li>
      <li>While you're on a streak, every win gives +10% XP per streak level, up to +50%.</li>
      <li>The results screen shows your streak progress, the operator card shows a 🔥 badge, and the career card and Account screen track your current and best streak.</li>
      <li>Every mode counts except the practice range. In Battle Royale only first place counts as a win.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.42 · HANDS</div>
    <h3>Real hands instead of blocks</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The square hands are gone. Every gun now has modelled hands: tactical gloves with knuckle pads, fingers curled around the grip, a trigger finger resting along the frame, a thumb, a wrist and a tapered sleeve with a cuff and fabric folds.</li>
      <li>On pistols the left hand cups the right. On rifles, SMGs, shotguns and snipers it holds the handguard from underneath.</li>
      <li>Hands are placed on each gun's own grip and handguard, so they line up on all 19 newer gun models.</li>
      <li>Your sleeves match the camo of the agent you have equipped.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.41 · FIX</div>
    <h3>P2000 fixed</h3>
    <ul><li>The P2000 was held backwards, with the barrel pointing at you and the grip under the front. It now points forward with the grip in your hand.</li></ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.40 · ACCOUNTS</div>
    <h3>Passwords, profile photos and multiple accounts</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Password:</b> new accounts now choose a password (6+ characters, with a strength meter). Existing players are asked to set one the next time they open the game.</li>
      <li><b>Recovery code:</b> when you set a password you get a code like ABCD-1234. Keep it safe; it's the only way to reset a forgotten password.</li>
      <li><b>Sign-in screen:</b> the game asks for your password when it starts. Tick "Stay signed in" to skip it on your own device. After 5 wrong tries you wait 30 seconds.</li>
      <li><b>Profile photo:</b> take a selfie with the camera or pick a picture from your gallery, then drag and zoom to frame it. It shows on the sign-in screen, the top bar, your operator card and the Account screen.</li>
      <li><b>Several accounts:</b> Account → ⇄ Switch lets you add more accounts and switch between them. Each one keeps its own level, coins, skins, stats, daily tasks and password.</li>
      <li>Account → 🔒 Password changes your password, 📷 Photo changes your picture, and Sign out locks the game.</li>
      <li>Accounts are stored on this device only; they aren't online accounts.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.39 · AGENT SIGNATURES</div>
    <h3>Every agent you buy is now special</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Sand Viper · Quick Hands:</b> reload 15% faster.</li>
      <li><b>Jungle Ghost · Fieldcraft:</b> after 4 s without taking damage, heal 2 HP a second, up to 60 HP.</li>
      <li><b>Night Owl · Steady Aim:</b> 15% less recoil on every gun.</li>
      <li><b>Arctic Fox · Swift:</b> move 6% faster.</li>
      <li><b>Crimson Fang · Bloodlust:</b> every kill heals you 15 HP.</li>
      <li><b>Gold Standard · Bounty Hunter:</b> 25% more coins and 10% more XP from every match.</li>
      <li>Each agent also has a <b>signature kill effect</b>: a burst of its own symbol in its own colour. Your lobby pad glows in your agent's colour, a perk badge shows above your health, and a short intro appears when the match starts.</li>
      <li>Health perks (Fieldcraft, Bloodlust) work in bot matches and rooms you host.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.38 · DAILY TASKS</div>
    <h3>Daily tasks: coins, skins and level boosts</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>New <b>Daily Tasks</b> button (calendar icon, top right). It shows a badge when a reward is ready to claim.</li>
      <li>Three new tasks every day, Easy, Medium and Hard, such as "Get 10 kills", "Get 5 headshot kills", "Win a Bomb Defusal match" or "Get 3 kills with sniper rifles".</li>
      <li>Each day one task pays <b>coins</b>, one pays a <b>weapon skin</b> and one pays a <b>level boost</b>: bonus XP plus 2× XP for your next 1–3 matches.</li>
      <li>Finish all three for the <b>daily bonus</b>: 300 coins and a rare weapon skin.</li>
      <li>Don't like a task? Swap one unfinished task per day. Progress updates at the end of every match (online too), except the practice range.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.37 · ACCOUNT</div>
    <h3>Personal combat analytics</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>New <b>Account</b> button (the person icon at the top right) opens your combat analytics.</li>
      <li><b>Overview:</b> accuracy, headshot kills %, head hits %, damage per match, K/D, total damage, win rate and longest kill. Each main stat shows whether you're improving: your last 10 matches compared with the 10 before.</li>
      <li><b>Improvement over time:</b> a chart of your accuracy, headshot %, damage or K/D for every match, with a 5-match average line. Hover or tap a point to see that match.</li>
      <li><b>Weapons:</b> kills, accuracy, headshot kills, damage, damage per hit and shots for every gun, knife and grenade you've used. Tap a column to sort; your best gun is marked.</li>
      <li><b>Match history:</b> your last 40 matches with result, K/D, accuracy, headshots, damage and top weapon.</li>
      <li><b>Insights:</b> short tips based on your numbers, like your weakest gun or how often you hit the head.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.36 · LADDERS</div>
    <h3>Real steel ladders</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The flat ladder pictures in Battle Royale are now proper 3D steel ladders: two rails, round rungs every 30 cm, brackets bolted to the wall, base plates, and grab rails that bend over the roof edge.</li>
      <li>Tall ladders get a yellow safety cage. It's hidden on Low prop detail to keep phones fast.</li>
      <li>Ladders no longer block doorways.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.35 · BUILDINGS</div>
    <h3>Sharper, weathered buildings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><b>HD walls:</b> plaster, stone, brick and concrete textures are now 4× sharper. Plaster has trowel marks and hairline cracks, stone has bevelled blocks, and concrete has form-panel seams, tie holes and rust streaks.</li>
      <li><b>Weathering:</b> walls get dirt and damp near the ground, rain streaks running down, and soft colour variation, so no two walls look the same.</li>
      <li><b>Corner stones:</b> plaster and stone buildings get dressed corner blocks. They're hidden on Low prop detail to keep phones fast.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.34 · LOBBY &amp; VERSUS</div>
    <h3>A new lobby street and home screen</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Street:</b> sharp sun-baked asphalt with cracks, patch repairs, oil stains and tyre wear, a dashed yellow centre line, stone kerbs, paved sidewalks, sand drifting in from the edges, a drain grate and a manhole.</li>
      <li><b>Deploy pad:</b> the thin glowing ring under your operator is now a painted deployment marker.</li>
      <li><b>Versus:</b> pick 1v1, 1v2, 1v3, 2v2, 3v3, 4v4 or 5v5. Play it against bots, host it for friends, from the Versus card in Play, or press ⚔ Challenge next to a friend to send them the invite. Kill goal scales with the size (1v2 first to 15, up to 40 for 4v4 and 5v5), and bots fill any empty slots.</li>
      <li><b>Career card:</b> rank badge, matches, kills, wins and a win-rate bar. The operator card has a cleaner XP bar.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.31 · SOUND &amp; SCREENS</div>
    <h3>Every sound redone, new buy menu, scoreboard and pause</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Announcer:</b> radio callouts for "Go go go", "The bomb has been planted", "The bomb has been defused" and who won the round. Turn it off in Settings → Game.</li>
      <li><b>New sounds:</b> buying gear (rustle and clack), denied purchases, pickups, the radio chirp countdown, the round-start horn, the C4 beep (a real two-tone beeper), the alarm klaxon, jumps, smoke grenade pop and hiss, scope zoom, weapon inspect, level-up, medals, and a win or lose stinger at the end of every Bomb Defusal round.</li>
      <li><b>Buy menu:</b> every item shows its picture and price. You can see at a glance what you own and what you can't afford, and your money is shown big at the top.</li>
      <li><b>Scoreboard (Tab):</b> the big team score, the map and clock, and both teams in separate panels with avatars, rank, kills, deaths, K/D and money. Dead players fade, and the C4 carrier is tagged.</li>
      <li><b>Pause menu:</b> shows your kills, deaths, headshots and accuracy, with big buttons.</li>
      <li>New toggles in Settings → Game: Announcer voice, 3D positional sound, Menu sounds.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.30 · 3D SOUND &amp; HUD</div>
    <h3>3D sound and a sharper HUD</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><b>3D positional audio:</b> gunshots, footsteps, reloads and explosions now come from where they really are, including in front, behind, above and below. Headphones recommended.</li>
      <li><b>Walls muffle sound:</b> an enemy behind a wall or inside a building sounds dull and quieter. Far-away shots lose their crack and become distant thumps.</li>
      <li><b>Rooms sound like rooms:</b> under a roof (B Underpass, inside buildings) you hear a tight room echo. Outside you get a long open-air tail and a slapback echo off the buildings.</li>
      <li><b>Low health:</b> below 30 HP the world sounds muffled and you hear your own heartbeat.</li>
      <li><b>Menu sounds:</b> soft ticks when you hover and click, and a different sound for switching tabs.</li>
      <li><b>HUD:</b> the score bar shows a tile for every player on both teams. Dead players are crossed out, your tile is outlined, and the C4 carrier is marked. A red arc around your crosshair shows where you're being shot from. The ammo box has a bullet bar for the magazine and turns red when you're low.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.29 · NEW GUN MODELS</div>
    <h3>19 guns get detailed models of their own</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>New detailed models with real textures for the Desert Eagle, M249, MP5, Thompson, Barrett, .357 Revolver, Sawed-Off, XM1014, Nova, Dual Berettas, P2000, AUG, M1A, UMP-45, Negev, SCAR-20, PP-Bizon, FAMAS and SSG 08. They appear in your hands, in the inventory and in the store.</li>
      <li>Gun models by Hobbeswyn. Thank you!</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.28 · EVERY GUN ITS OWN</div>
    <h3>Every gun keeps its own model</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Every gun has its own shape again. The guns without a detailed model are built from their real side profile, with pixel-style textures, outlined edges, rails, sights, muzzle devices and magazines, and are held at a three-quarter angle like the AK-47.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.26 · HD GUNS</div>
    <h3>Sharper, shinier guns</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Every gun and knife texture is upscaled with a pixel-art-aware filter. Edges and panel lines stay crisp instead of blocky, and stay sharp at an angle.</li>
      <li>Guns now have real material shading: steel parts catch a subtle sheen and reflect the sky and sand, while wood and polymer stay matte. Painted skins have a glossy finish, and 24K Gold looks like real gold.</li>
      <li>Your weapon is lit by a key light, a soft warm fill and a cool rim light, so it stands out from the background.</li>
      <li>Phones use a lighter version to save memory.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.25</div>
    <h3>Faster inventory</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The inventory loads 120 items at a time, with a "Show more" button, so big collections open instantly.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.23 · C4 &amp; BIG BOOMS</div>
    <h3>C4, bigger explosions, better fire</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The bomb in Bomb Defusal is now a real C4: six taped charges, a keypad, a green LCD, coloured wires, an antenna and a red light that blinks faster as it counts down. In the last 10 seconds the LCD shows the timer.</li>
      <li>The bomb carrier wears the C4 on their back, so you can see who has it. While planting you "type the code": the stars fill in with a key click each.</li>
      <li>Grenades, barrels and the C4 now explode with a flash, a rolling fireball, a shockwave across the ground, flying debris and a column of smoke that hangs in the air. They also leave scorch marks.</li>
      <li>Molotov fire has hot white cores and red tips, a flickering glow on the ground, rising embers and a light smoke trail.</li>
      <li>Fixes: on phones, "First to 40" no longer overlaps the score box. The B Underpass entrances now have a proper wall and lintel, and the lamps light the floor.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.22 · NEW LOOK</div>
    <h3>Cleaner menus, settings and results</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The Play screen shows every mode at once. Each card has its team size, round style and win condition, with Bomb Defusal as the featured mode.</li>
      <li>Lobbies show the room code as big tiles and list Blue and Red teams side by side. Each team shows its players, plus the slots bots or friends will fill.</li>
      <li>Settings are split into Game, Video, Controller &amp; touch, Crosshair and App tabs.</li>
      <li>The results screen has stat tiles, and its colour shows how you did: gold for a win, sand for a placing, red for a loss. You now hear a victory fanfare or a defeat stinger when the match ends.</li>
      <li>The store says how many coins you still need for a case. The controller layout screen got a cleaner look.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.21 · CONTROLS SCREEN</div>
    <h3>New controller layout screen</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The first time you play with a controller, a full controller layout shows you every move. It matches your controller: PlayStation buttons (✕ ○ □ △, L1/R1, Options) or Xbox (A B X Y, LB/RB, Menu).</li>
      <li>Press any button and it lights up on the drawing. The sticks move with your thumbs. Press Options / Menu to continue.</li>
      <li>Open it any time from Settings → Controller, or from the pause menu → Controls. On-screen hints now use your controller's button names.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.20 · CONTROLLER FIXES</div>
    <h3>Controller fixes</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Fixed the view turning by itself while playing with a controller. The mouse cursor sitting at the edge of the screen was turning the camera.</li>
      <li>Controllers that report their triggers as sticks (common on Android and with generic pads) no longer spin the view. Their triggers now fire and aim properly.</li>
      <li>Stick drift is calibrated out automatically. Settings → Controller has a dead-zone slider and a live stick readout.</li>
      <li>Picking up the controller in the middle of a match no longer pauses the game.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.19 · MATCH CLOCK</div>
    <h3>Matches end on time</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>On slower phones the match clock ran slower than real time, so a 5:00 match could last much longer. The clock now always keeps real time (also round timers and the start countdown).</li>
      <li>The results screen now says why the match ended: "Wolf reached 20 kills first" or "Time's up · you had the most kills".</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.18 · CONTROLLER</div>
    <h3>Controller support</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Plug in or pair an Xbox, PlayStation or other standard controller and press any button. It works on PC, in the browser and in the Android app.</li>
      <li>RT fire · LT aim · left stick move (click to sprint) · right stick look · A jump · B crouch, or slide while sprinting · X reload · Y next weapon · LB grenade · RB use / plant / defuse / pick up · D-pad ↑ primary, ← pistol, ↓ knife, → buy (heal in Battle Royale) · View for scores · Menu to pause.</li>
      <li>The menus work on the controller too: D-pad or left stick to move, A to select, B to go back, LB/RB to switch tabs. You get vibration on shots, hits and explosions. Aim assist turns on automatically for controllers, and on-screen hints show controller buttons.</li>
      <li>Settings → Controller has look speed, invert up/down and a vibration on/off switch. Moving the mouse or pressing a key switches straight back to mouse and keyboard.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.17 · FRIENDS &amp; 1v1</div>
    <h3>Friends, invites and 1v1 Duels</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>New <b>Friends</b> button (top right). Share your 6-character friend code, add your friends' codes and see who's online.</li>
      <li>Press <b>⚔ 1v1</b> on an online friend to challenge them. They get a pop-up to accept, and both of you land in a 1v1 lobby. In any Multiplayer lobby, press <b>Invite friends</b> to bring friends in.</li>
      <li>New mode <b>1v1 Duel</b>: first to 10 kills, spawning at opposite ends of the map. Play it online with a friend, or against a bot.</li>
      <li>Fixes: the Free-for-All leaderboard no longer freezes on the previous match's scores. On phones the compass no longer covers it. The sealed dead-end alleys and bare wall slabs are gone from the classic map, and bots now plan routes around buildings instead of getting stuck on walls and low kerbs.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.16 · GLASS &amp; AIM ASSIST</div>
    <h3>Breakable windows, aim assist, better buildings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Shoot a window and the glass shatters with a real glass-break sound. HE grenades and exploding barrels blow out nearby windows. Windows are repaired every round.</li>
      <li>Aim assist for touch controls, the Android beta app and new players below level 15. It gently pulls toward a visible enemy near your crosshair and slows your aim over them. It never works through walls or smoke. Change it in Settings → Aim assist.</li>
      <li>The flat green sheet on Lost Temple buildings is now real hanging ivy. The map doors are proper wooden double doors, and the outer walls have tiled stone with a base and a top trim.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.15 · CLASSIC LAYOUT</div>
    <h3>Classic three-lane map & explosive barrels</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Bomb Defusal, Team Deathmatch and Free-for-All now play on a classic three-lane layout: A Lane with long doors, Mid with double doors, Short A, covered B Underpass and a B window connector.</li>
      <li>Red explosive barrels around both sites, Mid, A Lane and Tunnels. Shoot one and it catches fire, then blows up. It chains into nearby barrels, and HE grenades set them off too. Barrels respawn every round.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.7 · COMBAT HORIZENS</div>
    <h3>New name, tactical gunplay & smarter enemies</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Combat Rival is now <b>Combat Horizens</b>, with a new logo and a golden-hour lobby.</li>
      <li>Every shot kicks: camera recoil, FOV punch and a low thump. Heavy guns aim and sway slower than light ones.</li>
      <li>Manual reloads: <kbd>R</kbd> drops the mag, <kbd>R</kbd> inserts a fresh one, <kbd>R</kbd> chambers a round. Hold <kbd>E</kbd> at AMMO crates to restock your rig. Settings → Reload lets you pick Auto (press R once) or Manual.</li>
      <li>Lean around corners with <kbd>Z</kbd>/<kbd>X</kbd> (last weapon moved to <kbd>`</kbd>). Sandbag cover on every map, and bots can only hit what they can see.</li>
      <li>Enemy classes: fast Rushers, armored Heavies with machine guns, and Tactical soldiers who throw grenades and fall back to cover.</li>
      <li>Battle Royale, Free Fire style: ride the plane and press <kbd>SPACE</kbd> to jump, dive with <kbd>W</kbd>, open your parachute and glide to your spot. Carry medkits and heal with <kbd>H</kbd>, and race to red-smoke airdrops for top guns. Win the match for a BOOYAH!</li>
      <li>New trees everywhere: leafy oaks, tall cypresses, big jungle trees with vines, twisted dead trees, plus bushes to hide in on the Battle Royale map.</li>
      <li>Bomb Defusal tactics: T bots take map control (A Lane, Mid, B Long), stage, then execute with smokes, flashes and mollies, plant and play post-plant angles. CT bots hold 2-1-2 or stacked setups, call out enemies, rotate and run grouped retakes with utility. Team radio callouts appear on the left.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.6 · MAPS & BLADES</div>
    <h3>7 maps, katanas, grenades & water</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Dunehold, Exclusion Zone, Lost Temple, Oasis, Pharaoh, Reactor and Vineyard, picked at random, with real sand textures and realistic water.</li>
      <li>Katana and Dual Katanas: hold right-click to block, and a well-timed block deflects bullets back at the shooter.</li>
      <li>HE, Flashbang, Smoke, Molotov, Incendiary and Fire Bomb grenades with real bounce physics. Slide with <kbd>Q</kbd>, and a backstab with a knife is an instant kill.</li>
      <li>Free-for-All leaderboard, round hotbar, new crosshair styles, and redeem codes in the Store.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.5 · REAL ARMS</div>
    <h3>Real 3D guns & knives, kill cards, starter kit</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>AK-47, AWP (with scope), Glock-18, USP-45 (with silencer), P250, Tec-9, MAC-10 and MP9 now use detailed 3D models with hand-made draw, shoot, reload and inspect animations and real recorded sounds.</li>
      <li>10 real knives — Bayonet, Butterfly, Classic, Karambit, M9, Push Daggers, Skeleton, Stiletto, Huntsman, Talon — with draw, three slash and inspect animations. 10 new ★ knife skins in the Store and the Horizens Elite Case.</li>
      <li>Every other gun borrows the closest real shot and reload sounds. New kill cards, skull icons and combo medals with their own sounds.</li>
      <li>New players get a starter kit: AK-47, AWP, Glock-18, Knife, Classic Knife, Bayonet and four Stock grenades (HE, Flashbang, Smoke, Molotov). The mouse cursor is hidden while you play.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">PATCH 0.4 · ULTRA UPDATE</div>
    <h3>Full arsenal, knives, finishes & sound</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>45 weapons: 10 pistols, 8 SMGs, 6 shotguns, 2 machine guns, 7 rifles, 6 snipers, Stun Gun — each with its own spray pattern, sound voice and reload sequence. Side-locked guns in Bomb Defusal (Tec-9/AK-47 for T, Five-SeveN/M4A4 for CT…).</li>
      <li>21 knives unlocked by level — Karambit waits for you at level 100. 30 blade finishes (Fade, Nebula, Marble Swirl, Scarlet Lattice…) in the Store. Press <b>F</b> to inspect.</li>
      <li>New sound engine: layered gunshots with reverb and stereo, staged reloads (mag out, mag in, charging handle, bolt, pump, shells), brass casings, surface footsteps, bullet whiz, hit and kill confirms.</li>
      <li>Medals & streaks: Double Kill → Ace, Killing Spree → Godlike, Headshot, No-Scope, Humiliation, Air Strike… plus damage numbers, screen shake and a slow-motion final kill.</li>
      <li>Levels 1–500, ranks to Combat Horizens at 100, and every mode playable vs bots or online.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tag">CREDITS</div>
    <p>3D gun models, animations and sounds by lolokeia (CC BY-NC 4.0); knife models and animations by Shidzuko; kill cards and kill sounds by GD656 — user-supplied, personal non-commercial use only. Sound clips by Guep and Bullfighter; knife finish tiles from a community skin pack — all user-supplied, personal use. Weapon roster and base stats for Thompson, Remington 870, SPAS-12, M1A, Barrett M82 (plus Desert Eagle, MP5, AK47 and M4 values; magazine size, reload time, range, fire rate, recoil and zoom) come from a gun data pack by Gamingbarn (gamingbarn.net), licensed CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, rebalanced for this game. Non-commercial use only.</p>
  </div></section>
</div>

